    <GaugingStation location="Easter Turnaig" name="Oykel" number="3003">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station in very responsive natural catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Natural channel control pre-1986. Construction of stone croys immediately d/s (Feb 1986) affected low flow rating significantly; relatively unstable gravel control remains subject to change after moderate flood events. Rating developed from current meter gaugings, simple extrapolation beyond. Peak flow rating revised in 2016 and one rating for high flows judged to be suitable for whole record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity-area station; 40m wide river section.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Nov-Dec 2010 flows considered suspect due to extended period of freezing conditions. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in April 2017 (WINFAP Files v5).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Natural flow regime with only small lochs in headwaters. Very responsive.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Catchment is typical Highland mix of rough grazing and moorland with some afforestation in middle reaches. Mountainous headwaters, often snowy in winter. Impermeable bedrock overlain by superficial deposits. Minimal floodplains.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Flows fully contained." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
